    {
      "id": "doc-1789814470192-zdbk",
      "userId": "usr-1789814470019-txmb",
      "userName": "Sarah Connor",
      "filename": "Acronis_Consulting_Agreement.txt",
      "mimeType": "text/plain",
      "fileSize": 1667,
      "pageCount": 1,
      "status": "ANALYZED",
      "documentType": "Service Agreement",
      "summary": "Analyzed Service Agreement comprising 1 page(s), 5 detected clauses, 2 timeline milestones, and 5 actionable obligations.",
      "processingTimeMs": 3,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-19T10:41:10.194Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-19T10:41:10.194Z",
      "content": "\nCONFIDENTIAL CONSULTING AGREEMENT\nThis Consulting Agreement (the \"Agreement\") is made and entered into as of March 1, 2027 by and between Acronis Global Corp (\"Company\") and Consultant (\"Contractor\").\n\nSECTION 1. TERM AND TERMINATION\n1.1 Initial Term. This Agreement shall commence on March 1, 2027 and shall continue through February 28, 2028 unless terminated earlier in accordance with this Section 1.\n1.2 Automatic Renewal. This Agreement will automatically renew for successive one-year periods unless either party delivers written notice of non-renewal at least 45 days prior to the expiration of the then-current term.\n1.3 Termination for Convenience. Either party may terminate this Agreement without cause upon providing thirty (30) days advance written notice.\n\nSECTION 2. COMPENSATION AND PAYMENT\n2.1 Consulting Fees. Company agrees to pay Contractor a monthly retainer of $12,500. Payment shall be made within 15 days following receipt of an itemized invoice.\n\nSECTION 3. RESTRICTIVE COVENANTS\n3.1 Non-Competition. During the term of this Agreement and for a period of twelve (12) months thereafter, Consultant shall not directly or indirectly engage in, perform services for, or establish any business entity that directly competes with the Company's cloud storage solutions in North America.\n3.2 Confidential Information. Consultant shall hold and maintain all proprietary business materials in strict confidence.\n\nSECTION 4. DISPUTE RESOLUTION\n4.1 Arbitration. Any dispute, claim, or controversy arising out of this Agreement shall be settled by binding arbitration in San Francisco, California administered by the American Arbitration Association.\n  "
    }
  ],
